An observation-family goal is immutable and is identified by category, exact
carrier IS_TYPE Claim, exact left and right HAS_TYPE Claims, and Context bridge.
A goal stores no selected rule, search state, source position, conversion cache,
or object witness.

A rule candidate points to one conclusion goal and owns ordered, typed premise
edges. Claim, child-goal, conversion, Context-certificate, and
Substitution-certificate premises are separate edge classes. No untyped generic
payload is accepted.

Family formation and family inhabitation are distinct. OBS_ADT_DISTINCT forms
an uninhabited observation family; it is not compiler contradiction. An object
witness is an ordinary HAS_TYPE Claim whose classifier is an observation-family
Term constructed by the later object-action phase.

Definitional conversion is meta-level evidence. Failed conversion never proves
object inequality. Compiler work items and residual obligations are not object
evidence and are never artifact roots in fragment version 1.
